Looking at the current code, I'll apply UNROLL optimization to the inner `j` loops within the compute phases. The `j_len` is `TILE_N=16`, so I'll use an unroll factor of 8 (which divides 16 evenly). The key loops to unroll are `compute_kj`, `store_C_row_i`, and the load/store loops for tiles. Array partitioning is already `complete` for the tile arrays, so they're ready.

The primary benefit is in `compute_kj` where two multiply-accumulate operations run per iteration — unrolling will expose more arithmetic parallelism.

